Description: fate/vvc: cover multilayer parser access units and timestamps
 Check the packet boundaries of VPS_A_3 and OPI_B_3, and of a derived
 OPI_B_3 stream with the highest layer removed from temporal ID 4.
 The latter exercises delayed AU output when a layer is absent.
 .
 Check timestamps, stream offsets and picture metadata through the
 public parser API with fragmented and shared input packets. Keep
 expected results in FATE references, separate from the probe.
 .
 Update the CBS remux references for the corrected AU start codes and
 container references for complete first-AU parameter sets. The NAL
 payloads and the container round-trip elementary-stream CRC do not
 change.
 .
 Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
 Assisted-by: Claude Opus via Claude Code
 Assisted-by: GPT-6 via Codex
 .
 Port to 9.0.2: tests/api/Makefile and tests/fate/api.mak: placed by 9.0.2 context (no api-enc-parser entries).
